From f85689c7f45c33363b4a31651d6b06b637ba8f0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?K=C3=A9vin=20R=C3=A9mondi=C3=A8re?= <kevin@localhost>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:58:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/57] vulkan: opt-in coalesced loads + tunable MMVQ rows for
 ROCmFP4

Both behind env vars (off by default), correctness 2440/2440.

- GGML_VK_COALESCED_LOADS: raw-u32 view of A so adjacent threads make
  aligned full cache-line transactions instead of 17/18-byte typed struct
  loads straddling cache lines. Measured: +17% prefill, -3.4% decode
  (shift/combine overhead dominates at batch 1) -> prefill option only.
- GGML_VK_MMVQ_ROWS: 2/4/8 output rows per workgroup for the vec-id ROCmFP4
  pipelines (spec constant NUM_ROWS). Measured: no decode gain (rows 4 ~= 2,
  rows 8 -2%) -> kept as a tuning knob.
---
